truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.6+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add node-local session broker daemon (truenas-plugin-broker) that holds
    one authenticated WebSocket per (host, api_key) pair and proxies
    JSON-RPC for every plugin invocation via /run/truenas-plugin/broker.sock.
    Eliminates per-process re-authentication from forked qm, pvesh and
    pveproxy workers (D2). When the broker socket is absent the plugin
    falls back to the existing per-process persistent WebSocket path with
    no behavioural change.
  * Ship truenas-plugin-broker.service systemd unit, enabled and started
    by postinst before pvedaemon/pveproxy/pvestatd restart.
  * Map this branch's tn_*-prefixed scfg keys to the broker daemon's
    stable api_* wire format inside the plugin client so the broker
    binary serves both this branch and the legacy api_*-keyed branch
    without modification.
  * See wiki/D2-per-process-reauth.md for design notes.

